{"id":"h4-07-e2","title":"Outbox, saga, CDC and workflows","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: dual writes, transactional outbox, CDC, sagas and durable workflows. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"the-dual-write-problem","title":"The dual-write problem","html":"<p><strong>Updating your database and publishing an event are two separate systems, and you cannot make both succeed atomically with a simple code sequence.</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">db.save(order)          </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># step 1 succeeds</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">kafka.send(order_event) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># step 2 fails (broker down) -> event lost</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Reverse the order and a crash after the publish leaves an event for an order that was never saved. A distributed transaction (2PC/XA) across DB and broker is slow and unsupported by most brokers.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 260 130\" width=\"260\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two writes, no shared transaction: one can fail alone\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"1.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Service</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Database</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka</text></svg><figcaption>Two writes, no shared transaction: one can fail alone</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> At 1,000 orders/s with 99.99% broker availability per call, you lose about 0.1 events/s, or around 8,640 orders per day with no downstream notification (no inventory reservation, no email). Small percentage, big absolute number.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> This is the reason Debezium, Uber's and Shopify's outbox pipelines, and the \"Transactional Outbox\" pattern (Chris Richardson, microservices.io) exist.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Signing a contract and mailing a copy: if you sign but the post office is closed, the other party never learns of the deal.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"just retry the publish\". If the process dies, no one retries.</li>\n<li>Proposing 2PC across Kafka and a DB as a casual solution.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"transactional-outbox","title":"Transactional outbox","html":"<p><strong>Write the business row and an \"outbox\" row in the SAME database transaction. A separate relay reads the outbox and publishes to the broker.</strong> Atomicity comes from the local DB; publishing becomes at-least-once.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">BEGIN</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">INSERT INTO</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> orders(id, user_id, total) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">VALUES</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">42</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">7</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">999</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">INSERT INTO</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> outbox(id, aggregate_id, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, payload, created_at)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">VALUES</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (gen_random_uuid(), </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">42</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">'OrderPlaced'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">'{\"orderId\":42,\"total\":999}'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">now</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">COMMIT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Relay options:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Polling publisher:</strong> <code>SELECT ... FROM outbox WHERE published=false ORDER BY id LIMIT 100 FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED</code> every 100 ms, publish, mark/delete. Simple; adds DB load and latency (about the poll interval).</li>\n<li><strong>CDC (log tailing):</strong> Debezium reads the WAL/binlog (see next section). Lower latency, no polling.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 804.8 68\" width=\"804.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"One DB transaction, then an async relay to Kafka\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M354.8 34 L410.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M354.8 34 L410.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M500.8 34 L556.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M500.8 34 L556.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M646.8 34 L702.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M646.8 34 L702.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Service</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"256.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Orders and Outbox tables</text><rect x=\"410.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"455.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Relay</text><rect x=\"556.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"601.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka</text><rect x=\"702.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"747.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Consumers</text></svg><figcaption>One DB transaction, then an async relay to Kafka</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The relay can crash after publishing and before marking, so events can duplicate: consumers must be idempotent (carry the outbox <code>id</code> as the dedup key; see the delivery notes). Clean the table periodically (delete after 7 days) to keep it small.</p>\n<p><strong>Gravity.</strong> Outbox is the pragmatic default: cheap, uses what you have, reversible. Alternatives: event sourcing (heavier model change), 2PC (rarely sensible). It breaks when the outbox table becomes a hot spot at very high write rates (consider partitioning by time, or CDC).</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Debezium's outbox event router; widely used at companies on Kafka plus Postgres/MySQL. AWS offers DynamoDB Streams, which gives a similar guarantee.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Writing \"to post tomorrow\" on the same page as the letter you filed; a clerk later mails whatever is on the list.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting that the outbox gives at-least-once, not exactly-once.</li>\n<li>Publishing directly from the request thread \"as well\", reintroducing dual writes.</li>\n<li>Ordering: concurrent transactions may commit out of id order; key events per aggregate.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"change-data-capture-cdc","title":"Change data capture (CDC)","html":"<p><strong>CDC turns a database's commit log (Postgres WAL, MySQL binlog, Mongo oplog) into a stream of row-level change events.</strong> Tools like Debezium read the log with minimal load on the DB and publish to Kafka, one topic per table.</p>\n<p>Uses:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Outbox relay without polling.</li>\n<li>Keep <strong>search (Elasticsearch)</strong> and <strong>cache</strong> in sync.</li>\n<li>Feed a data warehouse; replicate between systems; strangler-fig migration off a legacy DB.</li>\n<li>Invalidate Redis keys when the row changes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Config highlights (Postgres): <code>wal_level=logical</code>, a replication slot per connector. Monitor slot lag: <strong>an abandoned replication slot makes Postgres retain WAL and can fill the disk</strong>. Initial snapshot, then streaming; schema changes need care (Schema Registry).</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 628.8 130\" width=\"628.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Log-based CDC pipeline\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 65 L178.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 65 L178.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M268.4 65 L324.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M268.4 65 L324.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M414.4 65 L470.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M414.4 65 L470.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M414.4 65 L470.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M414.4 65 L470.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Postgres WAL</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"223.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Debezium</text><rect x=\"324.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"369.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka</text><rect x=\"470.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"543.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Search indexer</text><rect x=\"470.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"543.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Cache invalidator</text></svg><figcaption>Log-based CDC pipeline</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Orders table updates 2,000 rows/s. Debezium emits 2,000 events/s at about 1 KB (2 MB/s). Elasticsearch indexer consumes in batches of 500 and lags under 2 s.</p>\n<p><strong>Alternatives.</strong> Trigger-based CDC (slower, intrusive), timestamp polling (misses deletes and rapid changes), dual writes (unsafe). Log-based is the robust one.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Debezium at many companies; LinkedIn's Databus; Facebook's invalidation daemon on the MySQL binlog; AWS DMS; Netflix DBLog.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Reading the accountant's journal to know every change, rather than asking for the full ledger over and over.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ignoring replication slot lag and WAL disk growth.</li>\n<li>Assuming CDC events have business meaning; they are row changes, often leaking your table schema to other teams.</li>\n<li>Transaction boundaries across tables are not automatically preserved in consumers.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"sagas-for-distributed-transactions","title":"Sagas for distributed transactions","html":"<p><strong>A saga is a sequence of local transactions across services, where each step has a compensating action that undoes it if a later step fails.</strong> It replaces one big ACID transaction with eventual consistency.</p>\n<p>Example: place order. 1) Create order (PENDING). 2) Reserve inventory. 3) Charge payment. 4) Confirm order. If payment fails: release inventory (compensation), cancel the order.</p>\n<p>Two coordination styles:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Choreography:</strong> services react to each other's events. No central brain; simple for 2 to 3 steps, hard to follow when large.</li>\n<li><strong>Orchestration:</strong> a coordinator (saga orchestrator or workflow engine) tells each service what to do and handles failures. Clearer, easier to monitor, an additional component.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 922.4 68\" width=\"922.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Orchestrated saga with compensation on failure\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M296 34 L352 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M296 34 L352 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M498.4 34 L554.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M498.4 34 L554.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M686.4 34 L742.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M686.4 34 L742.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Orchestrator</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"237.20000000000002\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Order service</text><rect x=\"352\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"425.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Inventory service</text><rect x=\"554.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"620.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Payment service</text><rect x=\"742.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"826.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Compensate inventory</text></svg><figcaption>Orchestrated saga with compensation on failure</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Rules: each step and each compensation must be <strong>idempotent</strong> and retryable; compensations are \"semantic undo\" (refund, not delete); isolation is weak (others can see intermediate state), so use states like PENDING and handle with care.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Flight + hotel + car booking. Car fails after flight and hotel are booked: compensation cancels hotel then flight (fees may apply, so compensations are business operations, not rollbacks). Timeline per saga about 2 s with 3 steps; orchestrator persists its state after each step to survive crashes.</p>\n<p><strong>Gravity.</strong> Choose sagas only when data truly lives in different services. If you can keep related data in one database, a local ACID transaction is better. Moving between choreography and orchestration is a heavy refactor.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Uber Cadence (now Temporal) for trip and payment flows, Netflix Conductor, AWS Step Functions, Camunda, and Axon framework.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Planning a holiday: if the hotel can't be booked, you cancel the flight you already booked (and may pay a fee).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Compensations that can themselves fail with no retry plan.</li>\n<li>Non-idempotent steps.</li>\n<li>Forgetting timeouts: a step that never answers needs a deadline.</li>\n<li>Claiming sagas are ACID; they lack isolation.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"durable-workflows","title":"Durable workflows","html":"<p><strong>A workflow engine runs long, multi-step business processes with its state saved durably, so it survives crashes, deploys and week-long waits.</strong> You write the flow as normal code; the engine persists each step, retries, timers and signals.</p>\n<p>Temporal-style idea:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">@</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">WorkflowMethod</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">public</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> void</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> placeOrder</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(Order o) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  inventory.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">reserve</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(o);                   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// activity, retried automatically</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">  try</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    payment.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">charge</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(o);                    </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// activity</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  } </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">catch</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (ActivityFailure </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">e</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    inventory.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">release</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(o);                 </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// compensation</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    throw</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> e;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  Workflow.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sleep</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(Duration.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ofDays</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">7</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">));     </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// durable timer, survives restarts</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  email.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sendReviewRequest</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(o);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Engine records an <strong>event history</strong>; after a crash the code is replayed deterministically to rebuild state, skipping activities already done. So workflow code must be deterministic (no random or wall-clock inside; use the workflow APIs), and activities must be idempotent because they have at-least-once execution.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 497.2 130\" width=\"497.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The engine persists progress and drives each activity\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 65 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 65 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 65 L346 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 65 L346 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Workflow engine</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"415.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">History store</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"74\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"415.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Activity workers</text></svg><figcaption>The engine persists progress and drives each activity</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>When to use.</strong> Order fulfilment, onboarding, payouts, KYC, subscriptions with timers. When not to: simple fire-and-forget jobs (use a queue), or sub-10-ms flows.</p>\n<p><strong>Alternatives.</strong> Hand-rolled state machine in a DB plus queue (works for small flows, grows messy); Step Functions (managed, JSON/ASL, per-transition cost).</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Uber (Cadence), Stripe, Netflix, Snap, Coinbase (Temporal); AWS Step Functions; Airflow for batch DAGs (different purpose).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A to-do list in a notebook that survives anything: if you pass out, a colleague picks up from the last ticked item.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Non-deterministic code in the workflow body.</li>\n<li>Treating the workflow engine as a database for large payloads; keep payloads small, use references.</li>\n<li>Skipping idempotency in activities.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Dual writes (DB plus broker) are unsafe: a crash between them loses or invents events.</li>\n<li>Transactional outbox: business row plus outbox row in one transaction; a relay publishes at-least-once; consumers dedup by outbox id.</li>\n<li>CDC (Debezium on WAL/binlog) is the best relay and also syncs search, caches and warehouses; watch replication slot lag.</li>\n<li>Sagas replace distributed transactions with local transactions plus compensations; choreography for small flows, orchestration for clarity; steps must be idempotent.</li>\n<li>Durable workflow engines (Temporal, Step Functions) persist state, retry, and handle timers; keep code deterministic and activities idempotent.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}